## Model card

- **Name:** Qoduck
- **Short description:** A stealth model in Qoder's model picker whose identity the vendor has not disclosed. Qoder is an Alibaba-linked AI coding product (Qoder International / Qoder CN); community fingerprint guesses pointing at the Qwen family are explicitly unconfirmed and are not treated as identity here. No parameter count, architecture, context window, knowledge cutoff or benchmark has been published.
- **Provider / access:** Qoder International (web/desktop app) only — individual accounts on Free / Pro Trial / Lite / Pro / Pro+ / Ultra plans. Not available to Teams or Enterprise, and not (yet) in the Qoder IDE, JetBrains plugin or CLI. No public API route or OpenCode Console/Zen listing exists — verified absent from the live OpenCode Console catalog.
- **Release / knowledge:** first surfaced 2026-11-07 (Qoder docs + official @qoder_ai_ide post, Singapore time); release date of the underlying weights unknown; knowledge cutoff unknown.
- **IDs:** no vendor model ID published; it appears simply as "Qoduck" in the Qoder model picker.
- **Context window:** not disclosed (no verified public score/spec found).
- **Modalities:** not disclosed (an AI-coding-product chat model; text in/out assumed but not vendor-stated). "Thinking intensity" is selectable, implying a reasoning model — vendor wording, not a measured fact.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** Qoder Credit rate 0.5× standard; a limited-time promotion (2026-11-07 to 2026-11-11 10:00 UTC+8) drops the rate to 0.0× within a daily free allowance for individual users, including at maximum thinking intensity; paid subscribers get more free uses than free users. No per-1M-token dollar pricing published.
- **Architecture:** undisclosed (stealth).

### Raw benchmarks found

- Every benchmark row reads **no verified public score found**: no official parameter counts, context window, leaderboard scores or head-to-head results have been published, and community "fingerprint" / pelican-test posts are unofficial and cannot be treated as identity or capability confirmation (per the AICoder newsroom summary of the official sources).
- Terminal-Bench 2.1 / Tau3-Banking / GDPval-AA / Claw-Eval / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas: no verified public score found.
- GPQA Diamond / HLE / LCR / CritPt / AA Intelligence Index / Omniscience: no verified public score found.
- SWE-bench Verified / LiveCodeBench / SciCode / Vibe Code Bench / DeepSWE / Coding Index: no verified public score found.
- MRCR / RULER / GraphWalks long-context retrieval: no verified public score found.
- The model is explicitly time-boxed on the vendor side: "Qoduck will be removed when the promotion ends" (2026-11-11 10:00 UTC+8), and the vendor warns of peak-hour queueing during high demand.

